{
  "id": "JER.8",
  "number": "8",
  "bookId": "JER",
  "reference": "Jeremiah 8",
  "verseCount": 17,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "8",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "JER 8"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "8",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“At that time the bones of the kings and of the officials of Judah, as well as the bones of the priests, of the prophets, and of the other people who lived in Jerusalem, will be taken out of their graves. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Instead of being gathered and buried, their bones will be like manure lying on the ground. They will be spread out before the sun, the moon, and the stars, which these people have loved and served, and which they have consulted and worshipped. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the people of this evil nation who survive, who live in the places where I have scattered them, will prefer to die rather than to go on living. I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " Almighty, have spoken.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.3"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " told me to say to his people, “When someone falls down, doesn't he get back up? If someone misses the road, doesn't he turn back? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Why then, my people, do you turn away from me without ever turning back? You cling to your idols and refuse to return to me. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I listened carefully, but you did not speak the truth. Not one of you has been sorry for his wickedness; not one of you has asked, ‘What have I done wrong?’ Everyone keeps on going his own way, like a horse rushing into battle. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Even storks know when it is time to return; doves, swallows, and thrushes know when it is time to migrate. But, my people, you do not know the laws by which I rule you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "How can you say that you are wise, and that you know my laws? Look, the laws have been changed by dishonest scribes. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Your wise men are put to shame; they are confused and trapped. They have rejected my words; what wisdom have they got now? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "JER.6.12+JER.6.13+JER.6.14+JER.6.15"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Jer 6.12–15",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So I will give their fields to new owners and their wives to other men. Everyone, great and small, tries to make money dishonestly. Even prophets and priests cheat the people. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EZK.13.10"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ezek 13.10",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They act as if my people's wounds were only scratches. ‘All is well,’ they say, when all is not well. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "My people, were you ashamed because you did these disgusting things? No, you were not ashamed at all; you don't even know how to blush! And so you will fall as others have fallen; when I punish you, that will be the end of you. I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", have spoken.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“I wanted to gather my people, as a farmer gathers a harvest; but they are like a vine with no grapes, like a fig tree with no figs; even the leaves have withered. Therefore, I have allowed outsiders to take over the land.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8.13",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Therefore",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "…",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "land",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew unclear.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Why are we sitting still?” God's people ask. “Come on, we will run to the fortified cities, and die there. The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " our God has condemned us to die; he has given us poison to drink, because we have sinned against him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "We hoped for peace and a time of healing, but it was no use; terror came instead. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Our enemies are already in the city of Dan; we hear the snorting of their horses. The whole land trembles when their horses neigh. Our enemies have come to destroy our land and everything in it, our city and all its people.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 8:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Watch out!” the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " says, “I am sending snakes among you, poisonous snakes that cannot be charmed, and they will bite you.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.8.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.8.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
